# unifont: GNU Unifont as a BDF file, the fallback that ends every catalog
# font set. It draws every character that the sources before it lack, in
# 1 bit, Han, kana and Hangul among them. Its glyphs are 8x16 and 16x16, so
# a set whose cell is smaller draws those characters in vtium's built-in
# font instead.
#
# The file is unifont-17.0.03.bdf.gz from Unifoundry, which holds the Basic
# Multilingual Plane, decompressed: the font helper reads a gzipped file of
# 1 MiB at most, and this one is larger. It is a required font: you install
# it at the path below.
#
# License: SIL OFL 1.1, the option vtium takes of Unifont's two licenses,
# with the copyright line the file's COPYRIGHT property gives: Copyright (C)
# 1998-2025 Roman Czyborra, Paul Hardy, Qianqian Fang, Andrew Miller,
# Johnnie Weaver, David Corbett, Ælla Chiana Moskopp, Rebecca Bettencourt,
# Minseo Lee, Ho-Seok Ee, et al.
#
# References:
# - ADR-1204 D5: the fallback layer.
# - ADR-1204 D2: where vtium installs the file.

role=fallback
source=bdf:/usr/share/vtium/fonts/unifont-17.0.03.bdf
version=17.0.03
sha256=3dbf3ed14e63f69dcc36663092269b312494429ce5a4ddc3adab042b5a0909c2
url=https://unifoundry.com/pub/unifont/unifont-17.0.03/
